<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5087" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄμβων</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ωνος</span>, ὁ, 
			Att.
		 for 
			Ion.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄμβη</span></b> , acc. to <i><span class="en">
			Gal.
			18(1).340
		</span></i>, but Rhodian acc. to Bacchiusap.<i><span class="en">
			Apollon.Cit.
			1.7
		</span></i>:—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>crest</i> of
			a hill, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				103
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπ᾽ οὔρεος ἀμβώνεσσιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Call.
					<u>Aet.</u>
					3.1.34
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>rim</i> or <i>edge</i> of a cup (esp. of one that curves
			inwards), <i><span class="en">
				Eup.
				52
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ephipp.
				3.16
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Critias
				34D.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Lyc.</u>
				9
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b> (from
			similarity of shape), <i>rim of jointsocket,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				<u>UP</u>
				1.15
			</span></i>, al., cf. <i><span class="en">
				18(1).340
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γυναικεῖον αἰδοῖον</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Eust.
				1539.33
			</span></i> (so perh. in Eup.l.c.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b> in Cos, <i>steps, rungs</i> of ladder, <i><span class="en">
				Apollon.Cit.
				1.7
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>5.</b>
			<i>pulpit,</i> title of poem by Paul. Sil., cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>JHS</u>
				28.195
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Aspendus</span>).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
